{{!-- v3 Powers tab.

      SEVENTH AND LAST PART MIGRATED. 168 lines on v2, ten includes, one inline style, and — for a
      quarter of this world — nothing at all.

      WHAT THE CENSUS SAYS THIS TAB IS (add-pc-sheet-v3 D9c, measured over the 88 live PC actors)
      -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
      `mortal` is 25 actors, second only to mage, and `powertab.js:60` gives mortal `primary: []`.
      Its Powers tab is empty BY CONSTRUCTION — not because the character has bought nothing, but
      because the system declares no axis for the line. `mage` is 29; at the time this paragraph was
      written its Spheres and Rotes had both moved to the Stats tab, so a mage saw only Resonance
      here — reorganize-mage-sheet-v3 reversed the Rotes half of that (Rotes are back, first section
      on this tab) and removed Resonance from it entirely (moved to the Stats advantages column, D4),
      so a mage now sees Rotes, then any Wonders, and nothing else that this tab draws unless other
      sections apply. So the EMPTY STATE is not a corner case on this tab; it is the common case for
      several splats, and getting its wording right matters more than any layout below it.

      THE EMPTY STATE IS DERIVED, NOT TABULATED
      -----------------------------------------
      `getPowertype(actor)` (pc-actor-sheet.js:1038) already answers "which power axis is this
      character's", chaining `variantsheet -> splat -> game -> actor.type` and returning one of ten
      names: magic, discipline, gift, dreaming, death, edge, lore, scarab, exaltedcharm, power. It
      is what picks the tab's ICON today. `preparePowersContext` now also puts it on the context as
      `powertype`, so the wording is one key lookup — `wod.power.empty.<powertype>` — instead of a
      ten-branch `{{#if (eq splat …)}}` ladder that would have to be edited every time a line is
      added. `.github/scripts/power-section-check.py` parses the ten names out of `getPowertype`
      itself and asserts every one of them has a key, because a MISSING key here renders as the raw
      string "wod.power.empty.scarab" on a player's sheet and no gate that only checks LITERAL keys
      could ever see it (this system already has one such bug live — see gear.hbs on
      `wod.labels.notes`).

      THE WORDING IS HONEST PER AXIS, WHICH IS THE WHOLE REASON IT IS PER AXIS (D9b). Mummy Hekau
      and exalted Charms have an icon and a `getPowertype` name and NO section definition, no
      powertab entry and no create button — they render nowhere at all. Telling a mummy player "no
      powers yet, use +" beside a `+` that offers Disciplines and Gifts and no Hekau is a lie, and
      D9b says in as many words not to ship it. Those two strings say the sheet cannot hold them
      yet. The generic `power` string promises nothing about what `+` offers, because for a mortal
      the answer depends on `settings.game` (`CreateHelper.getActorGames`) and can legitimately be
      "nothing".

      ONE CASE THE DERIVATION CANNOT SEPARATE, recorded rather than papered over: `creature` (6
      actors) has no branch in `getPowertype`, so it takes the generic `power` string — yet it does
      have a `charms` section, declared in `powertab.js` and defined in `BuildPowerSections`.
      Distinguishing it needs a `creature` branch in `getPowertype`, which is a behaviour change to
      a function that also picks the tab icon — not something to slip into a template migration.

      CORRECTED 2026-08-05. This paragraph used to end "(D9c: `hascharms` is drop-only and there is
      no create button)". Both halves were verified against the source and the live world, and the
      first is no longer true:
        * `hascharms` is NOT drop-only. Task 9.1 derives it (`wod-actor-base.js:578`) from the items
          the actor holds. It derives from POSSESSION, though, so it cannot bootstrap: it renders
          charms an actor already has and can never turn itself on.
        * "no create button" is CONFIRMED, and is the whole remaining gap. `CreateButtonsPowerv2`
          (`create-helpers.js:1990`), the PC power-create dialog, has no charm branch at all. There
          IS a `buttons.charm` at `:3436`, but in the LEGACY `CreateButtonsPower`, gated on NESTED
          `settings.powers.hascharms` — a different schema that is `undefined` on a PC actor by
          design (`actor_settings.js:60-86`). Do not "fix" that by merging the two schemas; it is a
          live-world data migration. Add a charm branch to `CreateButtonsPowerv2` instead (task 9.2).

      THE TAB IS NEVER HIDDEN. `data-origin="power"` is the only in-sheet route to authoring a
      Discipline, a Gift or an Art, so a tab that vanished when empty would be a tab you could not
      use to make it non-empty. Same rule the other six follow.

      SHELL/ROW SPLIT (D5), AND THE ONE PLACE IT BENDS
      ------------------------------------------------
      Nine of the ten includes are shared partials, passed exactly the arguments v2 passes, in the
      same order: `power_shapes`, `power_realms`, `power_listpower` (x3, for gifts / simple / the
      two-column layout), `power_listmainpower`, `power_listpowerdots`,
      `power_apocalypticforms`, `feature_item`. Untouched, so a fix to a power row still reaches
      both sheets from one file.

      It bends once, in the `unsorted` branch: `powers.hbs:112-138` authors that row INLINE — a
      `.width-namebox` name cell carrying `data-action="powerSort"` and a delete icon — with no
      partial behind it. Duplicated here deliberately, with every `data-*` carried across
      unchanged (`data-type`, `data-object`, `data-rollitem`, `data-itemid`), because inventing
      `power_unsortedrow.hbs` would produce a partial that could not actually be shared: v2 needs
      `.pullLeft.width-namebox` and v3 wants a cell that reflows.

      NO `data-action` AND NO `data-*` IS ADDED OR LOST. This shell authors two `data-action`s v2
      authors — `itemCreate` (with `data-origin="power"`) and the `unsorted` branch's `powerSort`
      and `itemDelete` — and everything else arrives through the includes.

      WHAT CHANGES BESIDES THE EMPTY STATE
      ------------------------------------
      1. A TAB TITLE, in the content area, matching the other six. On v2 this tab opened straight
         onto a section banner and nothing on screen said where you were.
      2. THE CREATE CONTROL IS A LABELLED BUTTON. On v2 it is a 3x-scaled glyph floating in the
         corner carrying `aria-hidden="true"` ON THE INTERACTIVE ELEMENT ITSELF, which removes a
         working control from the accessibility tree entirely. The glyph moves to a child `<i>`:
         `css/wod.css:399` sets `font-family` on `.wod20 button` at specificity (0,2,1), beating
         `.fa-solid`'s (0,1,0), so an `fa-*` class on the button paints a tofu box.
      3. `style="min-height: 150px"` ON THE GIFTS BLOCK IS GONE — the tab's only inline style, and
         a floor that reserved 150px of empty space for a werewolf holding one Gift. D4: an inline
         width in a shell v3 rewrites is removed, not overridden.
      4. THE `.sheet-area.flex-columns` WRAPPERS BECOME `.v3-section`. `.sheet-area.flex-columns` is
         `min-height: 100px` (wod.css:735) on top of a `max-width: 880px`, which is the same
         reserved-hole problem one level up. --}}
<section class="tab {{tab.cssClass}}" data-tab="{{tab.id}}" data-group="{{tab.group}}" data-drop-area="true">

	<div class="v3-tabhead">
		<h2 class="v3-tabtitle splatFont">{{localize "wod.tab.power"}}</h2>

		<button type="button" class="v3-add" data-origin="power" data-action="itemCreate">
			<i class="fa-solid fa-square-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i>
			<span>{{localize "wod.labels.add.item"}}</span>
		</button>
	</div>

	<div class="v3-tabbody">
		<div class="v3-tabmain v3-powers">

			{{#if actor.system.settings.hasshapes}}
				{{!-- Shapes first, and separately, because they are Trait items rather than Powers. --}}
				<div class="v3-section">
					{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/power_shapes.hbs" shapes=shapes actor=actor config=config locked=locked}}
				</div>
			{{/if}}

			{{!-- Spheres are NOT here: they render on the Stats tab, under Abilities (v3/stats.hbs).
			      `preparePowersContext` still prepares their context via `addSphereContext`, because
			      the Settings tab's sphere-ordering list reads the same items.

			      Rotes ARE here (reorganize-mage-sheet-v3 D2) — reversing the earlier move to Stats.
			      They render through the section ladder below like any other power axis: mage's
			      `primary` list in `powertab.js` puts "rotes" FIRST, so the `template === "column"`
			      branch draws it above every other section a mage's actor holds. --}}

			{{#if actor.system.settings.hasrealms}}
				<div class="v3-section">
					{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/power_realms.hbs" realms=realms actor=actor config=config}}
				</div>
			{{/if}}

			{{!-- The section ladder. `BuildPowerSections` walks this splat's `primary` and then
			      `defaultOrder`, so EVERY section exists for every splat and `section.condition` is
			      what decides whether it draws. The six branches and their `../` depths are carried
			      across exactly: a `<div>` is not a Handlebars context frame, so wrapping a branch
			      changes no path, but turning an `{{else if}}` into a nested `{{#if}}` would. --}}
			{{#each powerSections as |section|}}
				{{#if section.condition}}

					{{#if (eq section.id "gifts")}}
						{{!-- GIFTS — grouped by rank, which is why this one is not `simple`. --}}
						<div class="v3-section">
							<div class="sheet-headline sheet-banner splatFont" data-area="gifts">
								<span class="sheet-banner-text">{{localize "wod.power.gifts"}}</span>
							</div>
							{{#each section.data.giftsByRank as |rankGroup|}}
								<div>
									<div class="headlineRow splatFont" data-area="giftrank{{rankGroup.rank}}">
										{{localize "wod.advantages.rank"}} {{rankGroup.rank}}
									</div>
									{{#each rankGroup.gifts as |item id|}}
										{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/power_listpower.hbs"
											item=item config=../../../config actor=../../../actor locked=../../../locked showclear=false}}
									{{/each}}
								</div>
							{{/each}}
						</div>

					{{else if (eq section.template "hierarchical")}}
						{{!-- HIERARCHICAL (Disciplines, Arts, Lores, Edges, Numinas, Arcanoi) — a
						      container row with its powers underneath. `.area-box` is kept: it is what
						      `power_listmainpower.hbs`'s own rules hang off. --}}
						<div class="v3-section">
							<div class="area-box">
								<div class="sheet-headline sheet-banner splatFont" data-area="{{section.id}}">
									<span class="sheet-banner-text">{{localize section.localizeKey}}</span>
								</div>
								{{#each section.data.items as |item id|}}
									{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/power_listmainpower.hbs"
										mainpower=item config=../../config actor=../../actor locked=../../locked}}
								{{/each}}
							</div>
						</div>

					{{else if (eq section.template "simple")}}
						{{!-- SIMPLE (Rites, Rituals, Combination Disciplines) --}}
						<div class="v3-section">
							<div class="sheet-headline sheet-banner splatFont" data-area="{{section.id}}">
								<span class="sheet-banner-text">{{localize section.localizeKey}}</span>
							</div>
							{{#each section.data.items as |item id|}}
								{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/power_listpower.hbs"
									item=item config=../../config actor=../../actor locked=../../locked showclear=false}}
							{{/each}}
						</div>

					{{else if (eq section.template "simpledots")}}
						{{!-- SIMPLE WITH DOTS. No section currently registers this template: Resonances
						      was the only line ever to use it, and reorganize-mage-sheet-v3 D4 removed
						      "resonances" from mage's `primary` AND `defaultOrder` (it renders on the
						      Stats tab now, under Fuerza de Voluntad), so this branch is dead code kept
						      on purpose — the `template === "simpledots"` case in
						      `BuildPowerSections` (item-helpers.js) still exists and still builds a
						      `resonances` definition (for the Settings tab's power-ordering UI), so
						      this branch stays as the renderer that definition WOULD use if any
						      section were ever put back on it. --}}
						<div class="v3-section">
							<div class="sheet-headline sheet-banner splatFont" data-area="{{section.id}}">
								<span class="sheet-banner-text">{{localize section.localizeKey}}</span>
							</div>
							{{#each section.data.items as |item id|}}
								{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/power_listpowerdots.hbs"
									item=item config=../../config actor=../../actor locked=../../locked showclear=false}}
							{{/each}}
						</div>

					{{else if (eq section.template "column")}}
						{{!-- TWO-COLUMN. `.item-column` is the shared class its CSS hangs off; only the
						      outer wrapper changes. --}}
						<div class="v3-section">
							<div class="sheet-headline sheet-banner splatFont" data-area="{{section.id}}">
								<span class="sheet-banner-text">{{localize section.localizeKey}}</span>
							</div>

							<div class="item-column">
								{{#each section.data.items as |item id|}}
									<div>
										{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/power_listpower.hbs"
											item=item config=../../config actor=../../actor locked=../../locked showclear=false}}
									</div>
								{{/each}}
							</div>
						</div>

					{{else if (eq section.template "unsorted")}}
						{{!-- UNSORTED — a power whose `parentid` names a container the actor does not
						      hold. THE ONE ROW THIS FILE AUTHORS ITSELF; see the header for why there is
						      no partial to include. Every `data-*` is v2's, unchanged: `powerSort` opens
						      the dialog that re-parents it, and the delete icon is the only way to
						      remove one. `.headlineNormal` and `.width-namebox` are kept so the name
						      still reads and still measures as it did. --}}
						<div class="v3-section unsorted-area">
							<div class="headlineNormal info-box">{{localize section.localizeKey}}</div>
							<div class="area-box">
								{{#each section.data.items as |item id|}}
									<div class="row">
										<div class="pullLeft headlineNormal width-namebox vrollable"
											data-action="powerSort"
											data-type="{{../../config.sheettype.mortal}}"
											data-object="{{section.sortAction}}"
											data-rollitem="true"
											data-itemid="{{item._id}}">{{item.name}}</div>
										{{#if (eq ../../locked false)}}
											<div class="pullLeft power-iconbox">
												<a class="pointer item-delete"
													title="{{localize 'wod.labels.remove.disciplinepower'}}"
													data-itemid="{{item._id}}"
													data-action="itemDelete">
													<i class="icon fa-solid fa-trash-can"></i>
												</a>
											</div>
										{{/if}}
									</div>
								{{/each}}
							</div>
						</div>

					{{/if}}

				{{/if}}
			{{/each}}

			{{!-- reorganize-mage-sheet-v3 D3/D7 — Wonders and Fetishes, immediately after Rotes.
			      "Wonder" is not a real item type in this system: it is an `Item` document with
			      `system.ismagical === true` (relics, devices, talismans, periapts, matrices,
			      trinkets), and `Fetish` is always magical by type — `ItemHelper.IsMagicalItem` is
			      the one predicate both this list and Equipo's narrowed table are built from, so
			      they are provably a partition of what `getItems` used to return: nothing is
			      dropped and nothing renders twice.

			      PLACEMENT: this sits OUTSIDE the `powerSections` loop above, not inside it, on
			      purpose. Rotes is the FIRST entry in mage's `primary` list (`powertab.js`), so for
			      an actor whose Poderes tab draws nothing else from that loop (every mage, absent an
			      unusual cross-splat setup), this block is the very next thing on the page — "Rotes,
			      then Wonders" without hand-coding a dependency on the Rotes iteration itself, which
			      would wrongly hide Wonders for a mage holding none.

			      Shares `item_table.hbs` with the Equipo tab (D3) — same row markup, same
			      `data-*`, only the source list and caption differ.

			      D7 — THE HEADER (AND ITS CREATE BUTTON) IS UNCONDITIONAL, UNLIKE BEFORE. Every kind
			      `CreateButtonsGear` mints is stamped `ismagical: true`, so this is now the ONLY
			      in-sheet route to creating one, and gating the whole block on already holding a
			      magical item would make creating the FIRST one impossible from any sheet control.
			      `data-origin="gear"` is unchanged — it still dispatches to `CreateButtonsGear`
			      (`action-helpers.js` `OnItemCreate`) — this is a second, separately-labelled
			      `itemCreate` control, not a merge into the `data-origin="power"` button above
			      (that one is `CreateButtonsPowerv2`, which has no Wonder/Fetish branch). Only the
			      TABLE itself stays conditional on actually holding one. --}}
			<div class="v3-section">
				<div class="sheet-headline sheet-banner splatFont" data-area="magicalitems">
					<span class="sheet-banner-text">{{localize "wod.power.magicalitems"}}</span>
					{{#unless locked}}
						<button type="button" class="v3-add" data-origin="gear" data-action="itemCreate">
							<i class="fa-solid fa-square-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i>
							<span>{{localize "wod.labels.add.magicalitem"}}</span>
						</button>
					{{/unless}}
				</div>
				{{#if (getMagicalItems actor)}}
					{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/item_table.hbs"
						items=(getMagicalItems actor) actor=actor locked=locked caption="wod.power.magicalitems"}}
				{{/if}}
			</div>

			{{#if actor.system.settings.hasapocalypticforms}}
				<div class="v3-section">
					{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/power_apocalypticforms.hbs" apocalypticforms=apocalypticforms actor=actor config=config}}
				</div>
			{{/if}}

			{{!-- Trait items placed on the POWER tab (`system.placement === "power"`), as opposed to
			      the ones the Features tab shows. Same `feature_item.hbs` row renderer, same
			      arguments. --}}
			{{#if (gt powertraits.length 0)}}
				<div class="v3-section">
					<div class="headlineRow headlineList splatFont feature-itemlist">
						<div class="largeBox">{{localize "TYPES.Item.Feature"}}</div>
					</div>

					{{#each powertraits as |item id|}}
						{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/feature_item.hbs" actor=../actor item=item locked=../locked edittitle="wod.labels.edit.othertraits" deletetitle="wod.labels.remove.othertraits" showtype=false}}
					{{/each}}
				</div>
			{{/if}}

			{{!-- The empty state (D9). `haspowercontent` is the exact disjunction of every gate
			      above — shapes, realms, the `powerSections` ladder (which is where Rotes' own gate
			      lives, D2), the magical-item list (`hasmagicalitems`, D3), apocalyptic forms and
			      power-placed Trait items — computed in `preparePowersContext` — it has to be,
			      because "does ANY section have a true condition" is not expressible in Handlebars
			      and a hand-written `or` over the flags would silently drift from the ladder the
			      moment a section is added or removed.

			      `not` rather than `unless` for consistency with the other six shells, and to keep the
			      gate readable as one expression alongside them. --}}
			{{#if (not haspowercontent)}}
				<p class="v3-empty">{{localize (concat "wod.power.empty." powertype)}}</p>
			{{/if}}

		</div>

		<aside class="v3-macrorail">
			{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/macro_icons.hbs"}}
		</aside>
	</div>

</section>
